Why Is Demand Increasing?
Water treatment requirements: Municipal and industrial facilities require reliable disinfection technologies to maintain water quality and operational standards.
On-site chemical generation: Electrochlorination systems can reduce dependence on bulk chlorine deliveries and simplify chemical storage and handling.
Industrial safety and efficiency: On-site production can help operators manage disinfection requirements while reducing transportation-related risks.
Water Treatment & On-Site Disinfection Technology Watch
Electrochlorination systems play an important role in water disinfection and industrial process management. By generating chlorine-based disinfectants at the point of use, these systems can help facilities maintain a consistent supply while limiting the logistical challenges associated with conventional chemical deliveries.
Applications include municipal water treatment, seawater treatment, shipping, power generation, chemical processing and other industrial environments. Technology developments are creating opportunities for more compact systems, improved electrolytic cells and digital monitoring capabilities. IoT-enabled monitoring and automated controls can support operational visibility and maintenance planning. However, market participants must consider installation costs, electricity consumption, electrode maintenance, feedwater quality and system-specific operating requirements. These factors influence the suitability of electrochlorination technology for individual facilities and applications.
